BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Inspired by the Land: Art at Bothe-Napa Valley State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T160000
UID:260608PuWDbxhJ8E6_yVP9M7xnIA
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the Land: Art in the Parks is a free community art
  festival held at Bothe-Napa Valley State Park during California State Par
 ks Week. This family-friendly event brings together local artists\, makers
 \, musicians\, food vendors\, and community organizations for an afternoon
  of art\, creativity\, music\, and outdoor experiences in the heart of Nap
 a Valley.\n\nExplore a pop-up art exhibit and makers market featuring orig
 inal artwork\, handmade goods\, pottery\, jewelry\, painting\, photography
 \, woodworking\, illustration\, mixed media art\, and more from local arti
 sts and creatives. Shop local art\, connect with artists\, and discover un
 ique handmade items while enjoying the natural beauty of Bothe-Napa Valley
  State Park.\n\nThroughout the day\, enjoy live music\, interactive worksh
 ops\, demonstrations\, and creative activities for all ages including wate
 rcolor painting\, tie-dye\, leaf printmaking\, face painting\, nature jour
 naling\, community art projects\, an acrylic paint-along workshop beside R
 itchey Creek\, and an Eco-Somatic Expressive Arts Walk through the redwood
 s.\n\nFood vendors include Mi Cocina\, Cheese and Crust Wood Fired Pizza\,
  and Roman Holiday Gelato.\n\nWhether you want to shop local art\, try a n
 ew creative activity\, participate in a workshop\, or simply enjoy an afte
 rnoon of art and nature\, Inspired by the Land offers a unique way to expe
 rience California’s state parks through creativity\, community\, and con
 nection.
LOCATION:Bothe-Napa Valley State Park
URL:https://www.napavalleystateparks.org/inspired-by-the-land
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Evening Programs at Bothe-Napa Valley State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T220000
UID:260608HRMwJ_eA2UipMlxpLs_zlw
DESCRIPTION:Summer Evening Programs at Bothe-Napa Valley State Park are a 
 seasonal series of family-friendly evening events hosted by Napa Valley St
 ate Parks Association and Napa County Regional Park & Open Space District.
  Held throughout June and July\, the series features a rotating lineup of 
 programs including live music\, karaoke\, outdoor movies\, trivia\, and mo
 re. Bring a chair or blanket\, roast a s'more\, and enjoy a fun evening in
  the park!
LOCATION:Bothe-Napa Valley State Park
URL:https://www.napavalleystateparks.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London Speaker Series: Tarnel Abbott - Jack's Great Granddaug
 hter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T120000
UID:2606089X2sLLV3W0ev5boAe-ll8A
DESCRIPTION:Jack London’s great-granddaughter Tarnel Abbott will speak i
 n an interview format presentation. A retired librarian who spent 22 years
  at the Richmond Public Library\, Abbott has dedicated herself to preservi
 ng London’s books and papers. She is also a longtime activist\, involved
  in numerous local and international causes\, and will share her insights 
 into London’s life and legacy.\n\nShe will be interviewed by Gail Yamamo
 to Seymour\, an environmental scientist and advocate for endangered specie
 s\, climate change adaptation\, and environmental justice. She is a third 
 generation Californian Japanese American.  Over the past 50 years\, Seymo
 ur has been a self-educated follower of Jack London’s history\, drawn to
  his adventurous lifestyle and humanitarian ideologies.  Gail treasures h
 er friendship with Tarnel Abbott\, Jack London’s great granddaughter\, b
 ecause like her great grandfather and grandmother\, she is genuinely compa
 ssionate and is a vocal activist promoting justice for all.\n\nThis is par
 t of a quarterly speaker series\, co-presented by the Jack London Society 
 and Jack London Park Partners\, in honor of Jack London’s 150th birthday
  year.  The series features a range of experts and scholars\, sharing ins
 ights into Jack London’s life\, work\, and legacy and his connections to
  literature\, photography\, and the Bay Area.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-tarnel-abbott/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
