BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cookout At The Vineyard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T000000
UID:260611qqMw_0RxGE-L9VQMJ53XCw
DESCRIPTION:Cookout at the Vineyard is a vibrant\, multi-day annual fundra
 iser that centers BIPOC chefs\, winemakers\, and creatives. Presented by T
 he Veraison Project\, a 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) nonprofit organization dedicated
  to advancing equity in the wine and beverage industry through education\,
  mentorship\, and apprenticeship opportunities. This event serves as a liv
 ing reflection of our mission. Just as VERAISON marks the pivotal moment w
 hen grapes begin to ripen and transform\, the Cookout at the Vineyard embo
 dies a shift from visibility to equity. Since its launch in 2023\, Cookout
  at the Vineyard has grown from a regional gathering into a nationally rec
 ognized movement\, drawing acclaimed chefs\, winemakers\, beverage brands 
 and cultural leaders from across the country. The mission of Cookout at th
 e Vineyard\, is to foster meaningful connections between wine enthusiasts\
 , industry professionals\, and aligned brands in supporting a vital cause:
  building a more inclusive and diverse wine industry. A Three-Day Fundrais
 er | June 11-13\, 2026 Thursday\, June 11 Mix & Mash at Overshine Wine Co 
 The Cocktail Mashup Lounge Experience 6:00 PM - 10:00 PM Friday\, June 12 
 Block Party at Kendall Jackson The Ultimate Fish Fry Picnic Celebration 5:
 30 PM - 9:00 PM Saturday\, June 13 Cookout At The Vineyard at Balletto Vin
 eyards The Flagship Day of Food\, Wine & Music 4:00 PM - 8:30 PM Join us a
 t The Cookout at the Vineyard \\(CATV\\) and be a part of something bigger
 . Your ticket helps us pay it forward to the next generation of beverage p
 rofessionals who are innovating and diversifying the way we enjoy deliciou
 s food and drink.
LOCATION:Balletto Vineyards
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain't Too Proud: The Life and Times of 
 the Temptations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T000000
UID:2606116V5NggwGH0GCjxbHxkckbw
DESCRIPTION:Ain't Too Proud is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musical tha
 t follows The Temptations' extraordinary journey from the streets of Detro
 it to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance moves 
 and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind the musi
 c: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success they ach
 ieved \\(42 Top Ten hits\, 14 \\#1 singles\\)\, and the personal and polit
 ical tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in Americ
 a. This thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betrayal is se
 t to the beat of the group's treasured hits\, including "My Girl\," "Just 
 My Imagination\," "Get Ready\," "Papa Was a Rolling Stone" and so many mor
 e\, with a book by award-winning playwright Dominique Morisseau \\(Skeleto
 n Crew\, Paradise Blue\\) adapted from Williams's 1988 memoir. The New Yor
 k Times praised the show as\, "Pretty close to perfect"\, with The Washing
 ton Post proclaiming it was "Dazzling and Electrifying." Ain't Too Proud i
 s presented through special arrangement with Music Theatre International \
 \(MTI\\). All authorized performance materials are also supplied by MTI. w
 ww.mtishows.com Music Theatre International gives Ain't Too Proud: The Lif
 e and Times of the Temptations a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\
 , authentic look at the history of The Temptations. Parental discretion is
  advised.
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
