BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T180000
UID:260515Y5I-Yf21z0--XLGmD1OVXg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\n**JUNE EXHIBIT: SUMME
 RTIME LIVIN’ EASY**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 1 – June 28\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gra
 y  and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show a
 nd the Gallery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery
 ’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Re
 freshments will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fi
 zz.**\n\nSonoma County artist\, **Nancy Gray\,** unveils new summer-inspir
 ed acrylic paintings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the 
 region’s beauty.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows
 . Drawing inspiration from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abou
 nd with interpretive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal colo
 r expression plays out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue t
 endrils of shade dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a 
 carpet of golden yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splen
 dor\,”amplifying the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dra
 matic contrasting role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play again
 st the purplish blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by t
 he landscape\, these works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  
 “We are blessed to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – ever
 ywhere I look\, I see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelo
 ng passion for art.  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country wi
 th its inspirational landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early
  years vacationing on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright
  color palette.  She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90
 ’s and continued to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.
   Gray exhibits regionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gall
 ery for five years.\n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June
  18 and 25 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features
  **Collective Expressions: 29 Years\,** a members’ collaborative show ce
 lebrating the Gallery’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an excit
 ing mix of mediums\, subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery
 ’s dynamic diversity.  Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich hig
 hlight our region’s beauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\;
  from sunflowers to roses\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller
 \, Schaffer\, Sumner and Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolp
 er’s stunning still-life\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charles
 ton’s jewelry\; abstracts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary
  complement\; figurative works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this cl
 assic to contemporary overview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso jo
 in us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART 
 NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community ev
 ent celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. 
  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Hea
 ldsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **ww
 w.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly 
 Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Pride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T170000
UID:260515WC-ye4BqlEu6Tqe4JXxNaQ
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Valley Pride returns for a full weekend of queer joy\, 
 live entertainment\, community\, and Pride in the heart of Sonoma Valley.\
 n\nThis year’s celebration expands into a three-day Pride weekend\, brin
 ging together music\, drag\, dancing\, local artists\, food\, wine\, commu
 nity organizations\, and LGBTQIA\\+ visibility across Sonoma. Sonoma Valle
 y Pride is focused on building queer spaces\, creating joyful gathering pl
 aces\, and bringing more LGBTQIA\\+ entertainment and community-centered p
 rogramming to the region.\n\nThe weekend kicks off Friday\, June 12\, with
  We Rise With Pride\, Sonoma Valley Pride’s first annual Concert and Dra
 g Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre. The evening features headliner 
 J. Graves\, a queer\, non-binary-led band from Portland known for their gu
 itar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and high-energy live performances. Blend
 ing dance-punk\, post-punk\, and garage rock influences\, J. Graves brings
  a sound that will appeal to fans of Yeah Yeah Yeahs and The Kills — rhy
 thmic\, electric\, and built for the stage. The night also features drag f
 rom Bay Area legends Kochina Rude\, Sonoma County native\, host\, and perf
 ormer\, and Tila Pia\, an infamous stunt queen who has turned looks from H
 awaii to New York.\n\nOn Saturday\, June 13\, the celebration continues wi
 th a Pride Dance Party at The General’s Daughter\, inviting the communit
 y to keep the weekend moving with music\, dancing\, and celebration.\n\nOn
  Sunday\, June 14\, Sonoma Valley Pride gathers on the historic Sonoma Pla
 za for a free community Pride Festival featuring live performances\, speak
 ers\, queer art\, local vendors\, food\, wine\, and community connection. 
 With a bigger stage\, more room to gather\, and even more ways to celebrat
 e\, the Plaza Festival is designed for friends\, families\, chosen familie
 s\, locals\, visitors\, and allies to come together in the spirit of Pride
 .\n\nFrom the theatre to the dance floor to the Plaza lawn\, Sonoma Valley
  Pride weekend is a celebration of queer artistry\, visibility\, belonging
 \, and joy in Sonoma Valley. Come ready to dance\, show up\, and be part o
 f what comes next.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/?utm_source=bohemian&utm_medium=soci
 al&utm_campaign=pride-weekend---2026-svp-pride-festival-&utm_content=svp--
 -bohemian
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sebastopol Repair Fair & Clothing Swap!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T160000
UID:260514jxO_LWd68EigoEl5cyBQOg
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a lamp\, small appliance\, textile\, or bike in ne
 ed of repair?\n\n**Bring it to the Repair Fair!**‍ ‍\n\nVolunteers and
  specialized repair professionals will be on-hand to repair**\\*** your it
 ems.  We ask that you stay with your item while it's being fixed\, so yo
 u can learn tips for future maintenance\, how to shop for repairable goods
 \, and even how to repair things yourself!  \n\nElectronics repair and
  beaded jewelry repair will also be provided at this event.\n\n**If you’
 d like to bring an item to repair\, please register the item here:** https
 ://www.reusealliance.org/rf-reg (Pre-registering allows us to prepare for 
 your item!)\n\nThis is a free public event.\n\nThis event will also includ
 e a **Clothing Swap**. Please bring clothing items and accessories (clean 
 and in good shape) to share and bring home something new to you!\n\n***\\*
 We cannot guarantee your item(s) will be repaired\, depending on the exist
 ing damage or breakage\, ability of volunteer fixers\, and availability of
  materials for repair. Note: we cannot work on microwaves\, repair screens
  on cell phones/computer devices\, or perform any welding/brazing\, but w
 e are happy to refer you to professionals who can. In addition\, the texti
 le department is not able to perform the following:***\n\n***Replacing zip
 pers***\n\n***Repairing shoes\, leather\, or vinyl materials***\n\n***Perf
 orming alterations (making garments bigger/smaller)***\n\n***Replacing riv
 ets/grommets***\n\n***Hemming certain fabrics (stretchy fabric\, sleek/lux
 ury fabrics e.g. prom dresses)***\n\n***If you are in need of garment hemm
 ing\, we require that you please pin your garment to the desired length be
 fore you arrive.***\n\n**Join Us!**\n\nDoes fixing things sound like a fun
  way to spend a Sunday afternoon?  Or want to help out in other ways?  W
 e need you!\n\n**Email volunteer@reusealliance.org or sign up here:** http
 s://www.reusealliance.org/rf-volunteer
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.reusealliance.org/events/sebastopol-repair-fair
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slow Journeys (CA State Parks Week)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T170000
UID:260513FDyzKXkt1UeF8Oekn8cJwQ
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbird\, the taste of a Douglas Fir 
 needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or wat
 ching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and insec
 ts in the grass? Each month \\(weather permitting\\) we will exp
 lore one or two of our three accessible trails-- the Creekside 
 Trail\, the Nature Trail\, and the Meadow trail. Suitable for al
 l levels and a range of mobility\, these Sunday afternoon advent
 ures will accommodate people using wheelchairs\, walkers\, canes\,
  young children\, parents with babies in strollers\, and those w
 ho just enjoy slow walks in nature that stimulate the five sens
 es. \n\nThis outing is free as part of our Annual California St
 ate Parks Week celebration but requires RSVP. Meet at the White
  Barn parking lot. There will be frequent stops and opportunitie
 s for conversation\, photography\, nature journaling\, wildlife vie
 wing\, resting\, etc.\, so bring your nature journal\, camera\, o
 r binoculars if you have them. Wear comfortable shoes\, a hat\,
  sun protection\, bring water and if desired\, a snack. Space l
 imited to 12. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-slowjourney
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Forest Bathing Walk (CA State Parks Week)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T130000
UID:260511P3LYzVSEMkKIBDkdh9DM-Q
DESCRIPTION:Have you heard about “Shinrin-yoku” or “forest ba
 thing”? Here is an opportunity to take a walk and experience 
 the practice for yourself. Learn techniques to maximize the healt
 h benefits and stress reducing qualities of this walking practice
 . Shinrin-yoku originated in Japan and is gaining popularity in 
 the United States for its documented health benefits. This practi
 ce takes a walk in the woods to another level. A centering and
  calming restorative practice\, it promotes balance and restored 
 vitality through a quality of presence and heightened sensory awa
 reness. Sugarloaf Ridge State Park hosts a Forest Therapy Series
  as part of its Park Rx Program the 4th Sunday of the month 
 \\(March through November\\) led by certified Association of Natur
 e and Forest Therapy \\(ANFT\\) practitioners. \n\nWe invite you 
 to join us on this therapeutic experience of sights\, sounds\, s
 cents\, touch\, and memory. The outing begins at the White Barn
  and meanders less than one mile from the start point in a re
 verie of introspection and connection to the natural world. \n\nT
 ickets are free for this outing courtesy of California State Par
 ks Foundation as part of the Annual California State Parks Week
  celebration. Wear layers\, comfortable footwear\, bring water\, s
 un protection\, and if desired\, a snack or a picnic to enjoy 
 after the event. Parking fees apply. Limited to 12 participants.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-shinrin-yoku
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mtn\, Pythian Rd-CA State Parks W
 eek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T110000
UID:260511J72PPUkGbkqr2eqVZpqoBg
DESCRIPTION:How it works: Every half hour\, our Shuttle will leav
 e from either Sugarloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center \\(maki
 ng a brief stop at the Goodspeed parking lot\\) or Hood Mountai
 n Regional Park’s Pythian Rd parking lot \\(with a brief stop
  at the equestrian lot\\). Make a reservation to ride to the o
 ther end of the trail and begin your hike\, or hike and ride 
 back. We recommend riding first and hiking back to your car aft
 erward– no worries about how long you take to finish your adv
 enture. The hike should take 3½ to 4½ hours\; the distance is
  about 7.4 miles one-way with approximately 2\,300ft of elevation
  gain. Bring at least 64 oz of water and sun protection\, as 
 the majority of the trail is exposed. \n\nIf you are riding fro
 m Sugarloaf\, the Goodspeed lot fills up quickly. If it is full
 \, please park at the main lot and pick up the shuttle at the
  Visitor Center \\(you will have to hike a mile back to the m
 ain lot from the bottom of the canyon/Goodspeed lot\\). If the 
 Hood Mt. Pythian Lot is full\, please park at the Equestrian Lo
 t\, by the Hood House\, in Los Guilicos. \n\nRegistration is req
 uired as there is only space for 5 riders at a time\, but you
  can ride on a space-available basis as well. There is no char
 ge for the ride\, the $10 reservation fee is refunded on site 
 the day of the event\, unless you choose to donate it to keep
  this service running. Dogs and bikes are not allowed in the s
 huttle or on Goodspeed Trail \\(the State Park portion of the h
 iking route\\). Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-satshuttle
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T170000
UID:260508pKxKjliHCE6WNMa84eJdhA
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
