BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Special Sgraffito Workshop with Visiting Artist Sarah Anderson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T210000
UID:260602cEdLRAUGHUu34Qz6ebDvEA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nMonday · 1 Session\n\nDate & Time\n\nJune 15\, 20
 26\n\n5:00 PM – 9:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 110\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\
 , Workshops\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistra
 tion Cost:\n\n$120\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$185\n\nprogram overview\n\nHey\, it’s Sarah Anderson! Join me for
  a sgraffito workshop on June 15th at the Sonoma Community Center. As a cl
 ass\, we will deep dive into specifics like surface design techniques\, us
 ing the elements and principles in clay\, underglaze vs slip\, whether to 
 glaze or leave the clay body unglazed\, how to control the work time of yo
 ur clay\, and much more. This workshop is for all levels\, beginners throu
 gh advanced. Materials will be provided for you during this workshop: carv
 ing tools\, underglazes\, and porcelain clay tiles. You are encouraged to 
 come with your own piece already thrown and trimmed\, still at the leather
  hard stage\, ready for carving! If you want to take your pottery to the n
 ext level\, let’s talk sgraffito!\n\nSupply List\n\nStudents will be pro
 vided porcelain tiles for practicing\, and are encouraged to bring their o
 wn leather hard pieces already created to practice carving.\n\nNotebook\n\
 nSnacks and Water Bottle\n\nSchedule for the day\n\n5-6 PM: Intro\, painti
 ng our tiles and getting pieces prepped for carving. Students are encourag
 ed to bring their own leather hard pieces to carve on. Test tiles provided
  by the studio will be distributed to each student. While drying\, we will
  go over the specifics on consistency of clay at different moister points.
  6-7 PM: Move into the surface decoration – bringing out books and examp
 les of patterns\, movement\, line\, and how I come up with my characters. 
 If tiles are ready\, starting this transfer process and practicing our new
  carving tools. 7-9 PM: Transferring images to the surfaces of our thrown 
 pieces\, if applicable. Moving on to carving the larger tiles and the thro
 wn pieces. Explaining the carving process in detail\, negative vs positive
  space\, applying secondary colors for more depth.
LOCATION:Sonoma Communiuty Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/sgraffito-workshop-sarah-an
 derson/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
