BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Art Playground
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T160000
UID:2606041XvQuBxGkkW3pkTIqYkhig
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nDive into the world of digital art without the steep lea
 rning curve! This course is a creative playground designed for curious min
 ds of all ages. We're ditching the complex technical jargon and focusing p
 urely on experimentation\, play\, and discovery. You'll get hands-on exper
 ience with a diverse suite of accessible\, easy-to-use software to bring y
 our imagination to life. Go from sketching your first digital illustration
 s to sculpting beginner-friendly 3D models and bringing characters to life
  with simple animation. Bring your curiosity\, jump in\, and let's make so
 me art!\n\nThis class is located in the Main Gallery. \n\nStudents bring:\
 n\nLaptops\n\nPAC provides: \n\nExtension Chords\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\
 nLije Morgan teaches animation\, 3D\, and game design\, and offers private
  lessons for artists exploring new media. Their work examines the power of
  &ldquo\;cute&rdquo\; aesthetics as tools of persuasion and subversion\, o
 ften blending 2D and 3D techniques using Blender. Passionate about storyte
 lling through games and animation\, Lije also creates live visuals for per
 formances and hosts Boiled Over\, a podcast featuring independent animator
 s from around the world.\n\nLearn more: \n\nwww.lije.com@lije.mo
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-digital-art-pl
 ayground?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Tide to Treasure: Creating Wind Chimes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260615T120000
UID:260528sIcZ6QNzQUie6xCdQwT_CQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nDiscover where art\, science\, and the natural world mee
 t in this hands-on workshop inspired by the oyster-rich landscapes of West
  Marin. Through close observation and creative exploration\, participants 
 will have the opportunity to explore cultural and ecological stories while
  transforming locally gathered driftwood\, oyster shells\, and natural mat
 erials into a wind chime or wall hanging. Blending art with natural histor
 y\, this class invites you to slow down\, look closely\, and create a mean
 ingful piece that echoes the textures\, rhythms\, and stories of the coast
 .\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\
 nSue Dedina is an experienced Interpretive Educator who has taught for CA 
 State Parks\, US Forest Service\, Point Reyes National Seashore Associatio
 n and museums. With a BS in Marine Biology and studies in art\, she seeks 
 to bring the worlds of science and art together. Sue is a working artist w
 ith a studio at Novato Arts Center.\n\nLauren Volk has an MFA from Otis Co
 llage of Art and Design\, and a BFA from Art Center College of Design. She
  is a professional artist who teaches throughout the Bay Area. She is owne
 r of LVolkart Studio in Novato where she teaches private workshops and cla
 sses associated with the Marin Museum of Contemporary Art. She has also be
 en awarded multiple teaching awards from Art Center College of Design.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-tide-to-treasu
 re?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
