BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Watercolor: A Gentle Start
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260616T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260616T120000
UID:260612QN7cEFbeE0CTwq6_nApsLQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nIf watercolor has ever intimidated you\, this welcoming 
 class is designed just for you. Guided by Nancy Ballard\, you'll ease into
  the medium with simple\, approachable techniques that take the fear out o
 f painting. Through relaxed exercises and encouraging instruction\, you'll
  learn how watercolor really works&mdash\;without pressure or perfection&m
 dash\;while building confidence step by step. Emphasizing play\, curiosity
 \, and small wins\, this class creates a supportive space to explore color
 \, brushwork\, and flow. Perfect for absolute beginners or anyone ready to
  let go of fear and finally give watercolor a try.\n\nThis class is locate
 d in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nNancy Ballard's love of art
  began in childhood\, when she first discovered the magic of brush and pai
 nt&mdash\;a sense of wonder that continues to shape her work today. After 
 a full life as a mother\, grandmother\, and corporate professional\, she r
 eturned to art following her retirement in 2006\, studying watercolor with
  Mary L. Harden at Strybing Arboretum. In 2009\, she was recognized as a M
 aster Artist of Botanical Illustration by the San Francisco Botanical Gard
 en Society. Nancy has also worked as a gallery curator and exhibiting arti
 st throughout the Bay Area\, sharing her botanical work in galleries\, win
 eries\, hospitals\, and nonprofit spaces while supporting environmental aw
 areness through art.\n\nLearn More: \n\nwww.nancyballard.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-gentle-waterco
 lor?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Binding and Building Your Sketchbook Practice
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260616T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260616T210000
UID:2606126AYUw3NaeU-NldMb9a70DQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\n&ldquo\;Binding and Building Your Sketchbook Practice&rd
 quo\; is an invitation to reimagine your sketchbook as a space of freedom\
 , experimentation\, and creative discovery. In this dynamic\, hands-on wor
 kshop\, you'll craft your own one-of-a-kind sketchbook using both traditio
 nal and unexpected materials&mdash\;then fill it with life through playful
  rituals\, inventive exercises\, and techniques designed to spark spontane
 ity. Explore tools that travel easily and dry quickly\, making it effortle
 ss to create wherever inspiration strikes. Leave not only with a beautiful
 ly bound\, deeply personal sketchbook\, but with a revitalized creative pr
 actice that feels alive\, flexible\, and truly your own.\n\nThis class is 
 located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nAsh Hay is a multidis
 ciplinary artist based in Santa Rosa\, California\, whose work and teachin
 g are rooted in curiosity\, experimentation\, and community. They serve as
  Printshop Lab Technician at Santa Rosa Junior College and founded the Son
 oma County Sketchbook Club\, creating spaces for artists to connect and gr
 ow. Ash holds a BFA from Sonoma State University and was honored with the 
 Creative Sonoma Discovered Emerging Artist Award. Their work has been exhi
 bited at the Sonoma County Museum\, the Contemporary Jewish Museum in San 
 Francisco\, and Neon Raspberry Art House in Occidental. With over a decade
  of experience as a teaching artist\, Ash brings a playful\, exploratory s
 pirit&mdash\;grounded in strong technical skill&mdash\;to every class and 
 workshop they lead. \n\nLearn more about Ash: \n\nwww.ashhay.com@ashhayart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-sketchbook-pra
 ctice?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
