DESCRIPTION:In honor of Pride Month\, this panel brings together transgend
 er youth and adults to share their lived experiences\, reflections on iden
 tity\, and what Pride means in today's world. Panelists will explore visib
 ility\, resilience\, and the evolving landscape for trans people today. Th
 e discussion will be facilitated by local author and mother\, Janna Barkin
 \, a passionate champion for transgender youth and their families. For tee
 ns and adults. Free\; no library card required.
