BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Secret Garden the Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T220000
UID:260610SCwBN5MBykmqeYakFwM9pw
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of wonder\, mystery\, and renewal.\n\nCinnab
 ar Theater presents The Secret Garden The Musical\, the beloved story brou
 ght to life with a soaring score and breathtaking storytelling.\n\nOrphane
 d and sent to live with her reclusive uncle in a grand English manor\, you
 ng Mary Lennox discovers a hidden\, neglected garden. As she nurtures it b
 ack to life\, she awakens something magical—not only in the world around
  her\, but in the hearts of those who have long been closed off to hope.\n
 \nThis enchanting adaptation by Marsha Norman and Lucy Simon\, based on th
 e classic novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett\, is a moving tale of healing\,
  transformation\, and the power of nature.\n\n**Performance Dates & Times:
 **\n\nJune 12–June 28\, 2026\n\nFridays at 7:30 PM\n\nSaturdays at 7:30 
 PM\n\nSundays at 2:00 PM\n\nLearn more at cinnabartheater.org\n\n**Locatio
 n:**\n\nSonoma State University – Warren Theater (Ives Hall)\n\n1801 Eas
 t Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\nRun Time:\n\nApproximately 2 hou
 rs 30 minutes\, including one 15-minute intermission\n\nRecommended For:\n
 \nAppropriate for all ages – perfect for families\n\n⸻\n\nCast:\n\nMar
 y Lennox: Violet Spears\n\nAlternate Mary Lennox: Serena Ridout\n\nColin C
 raven: Nathanael Koross\n\nAlternate Colin Craven: Joe Schulze\n\nArchibal
 d Craven: Ben Sasnett\n\nLily: Syona Ayyankeril\n\nRose / Dreamer: Katie V
 eale\n\nMartha: Nicole Stanley\n\nMrs. Medlock: Tika Moon\n\nBen Weatherst
 aff: Jonathan Spencer\n\nDickon: Beckett Hepp\n\nClaire / Dreamer: Natalie
  Burton\n\nAlice / Dreamer: Miriam Valencia\n\nMrs. Winthrop / Dreamer: Ka
 thi Brotemarkle\n\nAlbert / Dreamer: David A. Bradbury\n\nMajor Holmes & S
 helly / Dreamer: Noah Evans\n\nLt. Shaw / Dreamer: Corey Wilson\n\nLt. Wri
 ght / Dreamer: Mason Hunt\n\nNeville Craven: Zachary Hasbany\n\n⸻\n\nCre
 ative Team:\n\nJane Erwin: Director\n\nBrett Strader: Music Director\n\nBr
 idget Codoni: Choreographer\n\nElise Clark: Stage Manager\n\nJohn Sheridan
 : Assistant Stage Manager\n\nRoss Tiffany-Brown: Technical Director\n\nApr
 il George: Lighting Designer\n\nMateo Felix: Prop Designer / Co-Sound Desi
 gner\n\nDonnie Frank: Costume Designer & Hair/Makeup Designer\n\nPeter Cro
 mpton: Set Designer\n\nJohn Rustan: Dialect Coach\n\nLaurynn Malilay: Co-S
 ound Designer\n\nDiane Dragone: Executive Director\n\nNathan Cummings: Art
 istic Director\n\n⸻\n\nGetting to Sonoma State University:\n\nThe Warren
  Theater is located in Ives Hall on the Sonoma State University campus in 
 Rohnert Park. Plan to arrive early to allow time for parking and walking t
 o the venue.\n\nhttps://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Theater\, Located in Ives Hall
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open Farm Days Weekend 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T170000
UID:260610Bac56iGoz02iuXOm2Ge2BQ
DESCRIPTION:TOUR \\+ TASTE \\+ LEARNand explore our local agriculture Join
  us for the weekend as 20\\+ farms\, ranches\, producers and purveyors wel
 come you to experience our local agriCULTURE first hand\, out on the trail
 . TICKETS ARE FREE!!All guests must register to attend - registration is f
 ree & easy WHAT IS OPEN FARM DAYS WEEKEND?Open Farm Days Weekend is an up-
 close chance to experience and learn about our local agriculture through f
 arm visits\, tours\, demonstrations\, tastings\, workshops and more – at
  various farms across the SLO County Farm Trail.  This family-friendly wee
 kend is designed to be a “choose your own adventure” tour of the SLO C
 ounty Farm Trail. Ticket holders are invited to review each participating 
 farm's happenings and plan which farms they would like to visit\, setting 
 their own itinerary and pace to explore the trail on Open Farm Days Weeken
 d.  REGISTER FOR YOUR FREE TICKETSRegistration is required We are excited 
 to announce that our 6th annual Open Farm Days Weekend is FREE to attend! 
 To attend this year's Open Farm Days Weekend you must register - registrat
 ion is free & easy. Once you have registered please make sure to check out
  each farm's activites for the weekend. Some farm's activities may require
  a fee and/or additional RSVP made directly with that farm. PLAN YOUR WEEK
 ENDOpen Farm Days Weekend is a "create your own itinerary" tour of the Far
 m Trail. It is best to make sure to pre-plan your stops and route before y
 ou start the weekend. Things to note when planning your own Open Farm Days
  itinerary:- Each participating farm has their own activities and experien
 ces planned- Hours vary by location\, some may be open just one day- Some 
 farm's activities may require a fee and/or additional RSVP made directly w
 ith that farm Start here: Check out our QUICK OVERVIEW PLANNING GUIDE for 
 a quick rundown of who is doing what\, when\, and where to kick off your p
 lanning. Then check out our interactive TRAIL MAP: you can save farms to y
 our favorites and create your own itinerary that you can export out into G
 oogle Maps for handy navigation. Open Farm Days Weekend is presented by FA
 RMstead ED\, a 501\\(c\\)5 nonprofit organization helping to broaden aware
 ness of local family farms in our community and showcase the sustainable m
 ethods used to produce the food and products we rely on every day.  FARMst
 ead ED | SLO County Farm Trail's Open Farm Days Weekend is fiscally-sponso
 red by Ecologistics\, a 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) in San Luis Obispo\, California 
 and sponsored in part by CA Open Farm Passport
URL:https://www.my805tix.com/e/open-farm-days-2026/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
