BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RYAN WOODARD at FOPPIANO VINEYARDS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T180000
UID:260611IOQP9T7NMkiVffT2MbhtPA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Father's Day weekend on the Foppiano deck with a spe
 cial solo performance by rising guitar talent Ryan Woodard. Admission is f
 ree\, so settle in and enjoy the sounds of live music with sweeping Russia
 n River Valley views.\n\nWe'll be pouring new wines on tap\, with handcraf
 ted light bites from SoCo Cheese Boards available for purchase. Whether yo
 u're treating Dad or simply looking for a relaxing Sonoma County escape\, 
 it's the perfect way to spend a summer afternoon.\n\nThis is a FREE event 
 but RSVP's are encouraged.\n\nABOUT RYAN WOODARD:At 19 years old\, Sonoma 
 County singer-songwriter and multi-instrumentalist Ryan Woodard is rapidly
  establishing himself as a rising star in the music industry. Diagnosed wi
 th autism at age three\, Ryan found his solace and his voice through music
 \, defying expectations after being considered nonverbal until he was nine
 . His extraordinary journey took a definitive leap forward at age 11 when 
 he shared the stage with blues icon Buddy Guy. Since then\, Ryan’s remar
 kable talent and story have captured international attention\, earning fea
 tures in Guitar World and a gifted Martin guitar from John Mayer. Known fo
 r his dynamic\, high-energy live performances\, Ryan is driven by a singul
 ar vision: to perform in the world's greatest arenas and take home multipl
 e Grammy Awards.
LOCATION:Foppiano Winery
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/foppianovineyards/event/612076/foppiano-pr
 esents-ryan-woodard
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers: Rebecca Smith: Look Books For Writers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T133000
UID:2606115b3uAWlW2EC9kNXdx3GRVA
DESCRIPTION:**Redwood Writers General Meeting: Rebecca Smith: Look Books F
 or Writers**\n\nPlease bring something savory or sweet to share in our pot
 luck!\n\nThis beginner-friendly presentation introduces writers to the pow
 er of look books as a visual storytelling tool for novels and screenplays.
  We’ll explore how images\, tone\, character\, world\, theme\, and comps
  can help clarify a story’s emotional promise and make it easier for age
 nts\, producers\, collaborators\, and readers to “see” the project. Th
 e talk includes practical examples\, common beginner mistakes\, and a simp
 le starter template writers can use to begin building their own look book 
 with confidence.\n\n**About the Presenter:** Rebecca Smith is a Sonoma Cou
 nty screenwriter who writes high-concept\, character-driven thrillers\, sc
 i-fi\, comedy\, and drama about resilience\, identity\, and self-acceptanc
 e. With twelve scripts in her portfolio\, a Master’s in Organization Dev
 elopment\, and a background as a visual artist\, she builds cinematic worl
 ds where environment shapes character and pressure reveals truth. Her stor
 ies are designed to be emotionally grounded\, visually compelling\, and ac
 tor-attractive—pushing fractured characters to their limits as they unco
 ver the fullness of who they are. Creator of LookBookList.com. She also fo
 sters service dogs for veterans\, a commitment to healing and service that
  deepens the emotional color of her work.
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/june-2026-rebecca-smith/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cruzando la Montaña de Sonoma - A Hike in Spanish
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T143000
UID:260610neFHlYASdkONRysac7FG8Q
DESCRIPTION:El Parque Histórico Estatal Jack London presenta "Rutas y Ave
 nturas"\, una serie de caminatas gratuitas en español.\n\nEl sábado 20 d
 e junio\, únase a una caminata inolvidable —guiada en español— que c
 onecta el Parque Histórico Estatal Jack London con el hermoso Parque Regi
 onal North Sonoma Mountain. La participación y la entrada al parque son t
 otalmente gratuitas (se requiere inscripción previa).\n\nEsta caminata ex
 igente\, de 8\,5 millas (aprox. 13\,7 km) de recorrido\, ofrecerá las mej
 ores vistas del valle\, rodeado de secuoyas y robles. Se ofrecerán refrig
 erios y tentempiés para mantener al grupo con energía.\n\nLlegue a las 8
 :45 a. m. para registrarse\, de modo que el grupo pueda salir puntualmente
  a las 9:00 a. m. La caminata finalizará aproximadamente a las 2:30 p. m.
  Lleve suficiente agua\, así como ropa y calzado cómodos y adecuados par
 a el clima y la actividad. Se recomienda el uso de bastones de senderismo.
 \n\nSi tiene preguntas o necesita transporte\, comuníquese con Carlos Bar
 ragán al (707) 938-5216\, extensión 109\, o por correo electrónico a cb
 arragan@jacklondonpark.com. Hay una cantidad limitada de mochilas y baston
 es de senderismo disponibles para préstamo.\n\nEs necesario inscribirse c
 on antelación. Por favor\, regístrese en https://jacklondonpark.com/even
 ts/cruzando-sonoma/.\n\nJack London State Historic Park presents Rutas y A
 venturas\, a series of free hikes in Spanish.\n\nOn Saturday\, June 20\, j
 oin an unforgettable trek – led in Spanish - connecting Jack London Stat
 e Historic Park with the beautiful North Sonoma Mountain Regional Park.  
 Participation and park entry are completely free (registration is required
 ).\n\nThis challenging (*difícil*) 8.5 miles hike will include the best v
 iews of the valley\, surrounded by redwoods and oaks.  Snacks and refresh
 ments will be provided to keep the group energized.\n\nArrive at 8:45 a.m.
  for registration so the group can depart promptly at 9:00 a.m. The hike w
 ill end at approximately 2:30 pm.  Bring plenty of water\, comfortable cl
 othing and footwear suitable for the weather and the activity. Hiking pole
 s are recommended.\n\nIf you have questions or need transportation\, pleas
 e contact Carlos Barragán at (707) 938-5216 ext. 109 or via email at cbar
 ragan@jacklondonpark.com.  A limited number of backpacks and hiking pole 
 are available to borrow.\n\nAdvance registration is required.  Please reg
 ister at https://jacklondonpark.com/events/cruzando-sonoma/.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/cruzando-sonoma/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society’s Seminar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260610kouHWa8kPECDIQhtBJ-nuw
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Seminar\n\n With Lisa 
 Gorrell and Cindy Brennan\n\nHow to Develop a Research Plan with Lisa Gorr
 ell\n\nFinding your Railroad Ties with Cindy Brennan\n\n Saturday\, June 
 20th\n\n FREE\n\n 1:00pm—4:00pm PDT\n\n Virtual via Zoom login beginn
 ing at 12:30 p.m.\n\nIn person come by noon and enjoy some light refreshme
 nts\n\n **1:00-2:00 How to Develop a Research Plan with Lisa Gorrell**\n\
 n Do you feel like your research results go in circles\, that you keep fin
 ding the same information\, or you have brick walls you cannot solve? Lisa
  will explain how to create and use a research plan which will keep you fo
 cused on your research.\n\n Lisa S. Gorrell is a Certified Genealogist an
 d has served on boards of several genealogical societies including the Son
 oma County Genealogical Society.\n\n **2:00-2:30 Interactive Break**\n\n
  **2:30-3:30 Finding your Railroad Ties with Cindy Brennan**\n\n There a
 re only a few things that are as entwined with American history as the Rai
 lroad. For many of our ancestors\, trains represented the most profound ch
 ange in their lifetime. New careers\, travel\, food\, medicine and product
 s that were never available before\, were now a possibility. Join us on a 
 virtual train trip to learn how your family was connected to the magic of 
 the Railroad.\n\n Cindy Brennan has been an avid family history researche
 r for over 20 years. Since 2009\, she has served as the editor of the Sono
 ma County Genealogy Society's monthly newsletter.  \n\n This meeting is
  held in-person at the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints in the 
 Cultural Hall\, 1725 Peterson Lane\, Santa Rosa or you can attend via Zoom
 .\n\n Even if you are attending in person you must register at **https://
 www.scgsonline.org**\n\n Registration closes Friday\, June 19th
LOCATION:Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints 
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
