DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T120000
UID:260413vE50F3Mfd0m2KbUI7ARkAg
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe series costs $80 \\(plus a $10 parking fee per vi
 sit. Note that the Sugarloaf Annual Pass is $59 and valid at S
 ugarloaf and Jack London SHP\\)\, or free-of-cost for participants
  with a March 2026 or newer Park Rx from a Sonoma County Medi
 cal Provider. Click https://sugarloafpark.org/activities/parks-rx-progr
 am/ for information on our Park Rx program and to download the
  form. The number of available Park Rx tickets is limited\; plea
 se have your Rx ready at the time of sign up.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/park-rx-beginner-hiking
 -for-fitness-spring-2026/18558541/2026-06-20T08
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain't Too Proud: The Life and Times of 
 the Temp.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T220000
UID:260330KakPPznGZ0a-P51SBzjfdQ
DESCRIPTION:Ain’t Too Proud is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musical 
 that follows The Temptations’ extraordinary journey from the streets of 
 Detroit to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance m
 oves and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind the
  music: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success the
 y achieved \\(42 Top Ten hits\, 14 \\#1 singles\\)\, and the personal and 
 political tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in A
 merica.\n\nThis thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betray
 al is set to the beat of the group’s treasured hits\, including “My Gi
 rl\,” “Just My Imagination\,” “Get Ready\,” “Papa Was a Rollin
 g Stone” and so many more\, with a book by award-winning playwright Domi
 nique Morisseau \\(Skeleton Crew\, Paradise Blue\\) adapted from Williams
 ’s 1988 memoir. The New York Times praised the show as\, “Pretty clos
 e to perfect”\, with The Washington Post proclaiming it was “Dazzling 
 and Electrifying.”\n\nAin’t Too Proud is presented through special ar
 rangement with Music Theatre International \\(MTI\\). All authorized perfo
 rmance materials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com\n\nMusic Thea
 tre International gives Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times of the Tempt
 ations a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\, authentic look at the
  history of The Temptations. Parental discretion is advised.
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/broadway-under-the-star
 s-ain-t-too-proud-the-life-and-times-of-the-temp/18460828/2026-06-20T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MIDNITE HELLION & Anvil
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T000000
UID:260327j1UybX3qOEKz8ouykuV2PQ
DESCRIPTION:Heavy Metal Rock 'n Roll - MIDNITE HELLION does it best.  Form
 ed by drummer Drew Rizzo and combined with bassist and vocalist Rich Kubik
 \, they create the power to amplify every town.  Their distinctive style 
 – classic\, no-frills heavy metal serving tremendously infectious spurts
  of thrash riffs with a straight\, fun stage attitude – made the guys a 
 top pick for world-class acts to ignite their respective crowds. Bringing 
 their strong regional fan base to the table\, MIDNITE HELLION shared the s
 tages with OverKill\, Dirkschneider\, Grim Reaper\, Flotsam & Jetsam\, Obi
 tuary\, Diamond Head\, Raven\, Exodus\, Yngwie Malmsteen\, and many more.\
 n\nTheir electrifying debut album Condemned to Hell \\(2017\\) proved to b
 e just the kind of wrecking ball that the band needed. Picked up and widel
 y spread by multiple Marconi award holder WSOU 89.5 FM\, the album success
 fully leveled a solid path into the wider US metal scene. In less than a y
 ear\,  Condemned To Hell became a national phenomenon – and so did MIDNI
 TE HELLION as a touring act\, spawning intense mosh pits left\, right\, an
 d center. The touring cycle in support of the album peaked in late 2018 wh
 en the band shared stages with OTEP and THE WORLD OVER in the Midwest and 
 Mountain regions of the United States.\n\nFueled by the sheer awesomeness 
 of their fans and the energy received from this crowd\, and driven by a ba
 g of new songs and ideas that they brought back home\, MIDNITE HELLION ent
 ered Pyramid Sound Studios in Ithaca\, NY in August 2019. The recording of
  their second album Kingdom Immortal took them only six days with the help
  of iconic producer Alex Perialas\, who in the past contributed to shaping
  the signature thrash sound of Anthrax/S.O.D\, OverKill or Testament\, whi
 le also adding a pound or two to Joe Bonamassa’s music.\n\nMixing took p
 lace in March and Mastering in May 2021\, before the vinyl mastering got c
 ut at Infrasonic Sound by Daniel Bacigalupi \\(Barry Gibb\, Dolly Parton\,
  Stray Cats\, Willie Nelson\\).\n\nKingdom Immortal became successful with
  radio stations in the United States from the get-go\, landing within the 
 top 5 added albums on radio throughout the nation.\n\nAs a result\, MIDNIT
 E HELLION toured the US with Anvil in summer 2022 for 39 dates\, supportin
 g the album\, followed by a second US leg with Anvil for an additional 25 
 dates in spring 2023.\n\nSet out for the first world-wide release includin
 g Europe\, MIDNITE HELLION hit the road for an extensive US\\+Canada tour 
 with German metal machine U.D.O. in the fall of 2024. The blast from the p
 ast is far from over!
LOCATION:Arlene Francis Center for Spirit\, Art\, and Politics
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108093071?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
