UID:260206TOPmy41e8UqMLOWhCcDviw
DESCRIPTION:*Where unforgettable wines\, live music\, and good vibes come 
 together.*\n\n Join us every Saturday from 3–6 PM at Spicy Vines for a t
 asting room experience like no other — where top local musicians from ac
 ross the Bay Area meet our award-winning small-lot wines. From Rock & Roll
  and Blues to Jazz\, Bluegrass\, and Americana\, each weekend brings new s
 ounds and new reasons to raise a glass. \n\n**Lindsay Gang** Lindsay Gang
  is a dynamic singer-songwriter whose music blends folk\, rock\, and Amer
 icana with compelling storytelling and rich vocal expression. Known for he
 artfelt lyrics and engaging performances\, Lindsay brings energy and emoti
 onal depth to every stage\, creating moments that draw listeners into the 
 song and leave a lasting impression.\n\n**Details**\n\nNo cover. Walk-ins 
 are welcome\, but this event tends to fill up quickly\, so we recommend ma
 king a reservation. We are dog and family friendly!
LOCATION:Spicy Vines Winery
URL:https://spicyvines.com/event/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River High Tide Upstream Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T210000
UID:260129SIA3E2hd_kq_aX5gteHr-g
DESCRIPTION:When the tide is high\, the Petaluma River opens into a quiete
 r\, greener world.\n\nJoin The Floathouse crew for a gentle\, guided paddl
 e upstream\, timed to higher tides that allow access beyond the downtown c
 hannel and into a tranquil tidal slough. With extra water beneath us\, we
 ’re able to glide into calm\, lush stretches of the river that are norma
 lly out of reach.\n\nThis unhurried paddle highlights the natural beauty o
 f the Petaluma River’s brackish\, tidal waterway. Watch for great egrets
 \, blue herons\, snowy egrets\, turtles basking along the banks\, and abun
 dant plant life. The calm water and peaceful surroundings create a deeply 
 grounding experience—many guests say they feel their stress melt away wi
 thin minutes.\n\nAlong the way\, knowledgeable guides share stories of the
  river’s ecology and human history\, offering insight into how this uppe
 r channel has shaped—and continues to shape—Petaluma. It’s a rare op
 portunity to experience how close wild nature lives to the heart of downto
 wn.\n\nBeginner-friendly. Sit-on-top kayaks and all gear provided.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/petaluma-river-high-tid
 e-upstream-paddle/17972590/2026-06-20T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BALLET FILM:  Peter I. Tschaikowski - Leipzig Opera Ballet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T150000
UID:260113-xGJUsH6V02Lr_8OdXbhrg
DESCRIPTION:A ballet by Cayetano Soto & Dario Suša \n\nA dance 
 story about Tchaikovsky\, illuminating the long-hidden moments of 
 his life. Through his compositions\, Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky influ
 enced and shaped classical ballet like  few other composers. The
  myth of his music remains unbroken to this day. Cayetano Soto
  draws an engaging portrait of a man who could not live his l
 ife the way he wanted to. In "Tchaikovsky"\, the view behind th
 e glorious moments of a  biography is revealed - in brokenness\,
  courage and genius. \n\nRecorded at the Leipzig Opera
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/ballet-film-peter-i-tsc
 haikowski-leipzig-opera-ballet/17866548/2026-06-20T13
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
