BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Draw Like An Imagineer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T120000
UID:260612R4IIb-YOnkOluAHlAnFJlw
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nEnter into a playful\, behind-the-scenes drawing worksho
 p inspired by real-world Walt Disney Imagineering techniques\, led by arti
 st and former Imagineer Maggie Parr. Through fun\, guided exercises\, you'
 ll explore how storytelling and drawing come together to build imaginative
  worlds&mdash\;learning to sketch from your imagination\, think in three d
 imensions\, and bring ideas to life with creative problem-solving. Blendin
 g professional insight with a relaxed\, inspiring atmosphere\, this worksh
 op invites artists and curious creatives of all levels to experiment\, pla
 y\, and discover new ways of seeing\, thinking\, and creating.\n\nThis wor
 kshop is located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nMaggie Parr 
 began her career at Walt Disney Imagineering\, working as a show designer 
 on attractions for Toontown and Animal Kingdom. After leaving Disney to fo
 cus on painting\, she continued as an independent contractor while expandi
 ng into book illustration\, murals\, portraits\, comics\, and television w
 riting. She trained in classical painting with artists including Steve Hus
 ton\, Cheryl Kline\, Steven Assael\, Jeremy Lipking\, and Joseph Q. Daily\
 , later earning an MFA. She now teaches students of all levels while maint
 aining an active painting practice.\n\nLearn More: \n\nwww.maggieparr.comw
 ww.parrcreate.com@maggieparrart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-draw-like-an-i
 magineer?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
