DESCRIPTION:Step into a creative afternoon at Montgomery Village with a ha
 nds-on workshop led by natural dyer and educator Lisa Rogers of SlowDigz. 
 This botanical-focused experience invites guests to explore the art of nat
 ural dyeing using fresh and dried flowers to create one-of-a-kind textiles
 .\n\nGuided by a spirit of creativity and discovery\, this workshop offers
  a relaxed and welcoming environment for both beginners and those looking 
 to deepen their craft.\n\nDuring the workshop\, guests will:\n\nCreate a f
 lower-printed silk bandana using fresh and dried botanicals. Enjoy a mini 
 Tataki Zome (flower and leaf pounding) demonstration while pieces steam. L
 earn about fabric preparation techniques\, including mordanting and scouri
 ng.\n\nThe workshop fee includes all materials and instruction.\n\nDetails
 :$55 per person\, 90-minute session\, Maximum of 12 participants\, Held ou
 tdoors (undercover) at Made Local Marketplace.\n\nAdvance registration req
 uired. Space is limited\, and a minimum of four participants is required. 
 A minimum of 72 hours’ notice is needed for partial refunds.
