BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T193000
UID:2604156q25o4AexEyzaE8NbKnVYg
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain't Too Proud: The Life and Times of 
 the Temp.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T220000
UID:260330C1gtuYxqXEaTCn8f6RV2Hw
DESCRIPTION:Ain’t Too Proud is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musical 
 that follows The Temptations’ extraordinary journey from the streets of 
 Detroit to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance m
 oves and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind the
  music: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success the
 y achieved \\(42 Top Ten hits\, 14 \\#1 singles\\)\, and the personal and 
 political tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in A
 merica.\n\nThis thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betray
 al is set to the beat of the group’s treasured hits\, including “My Gi
 rl\,” “Just My Imagination\,” “Get Ready\,” “Papa Was a Rollin
 g Stone” and so many more\, with a book by award-winning playwright Domi
 nique Morisseau \\(Skeleton Crew\, Paradise Blue\\) adapted from Williams
 ’s 1988 memoir. The New York Times praised the show as\, “Pretty clos
 e to perfect”\, with The Washington Post proclaiming it was “Dazzling 
 and Electrifying.”\n\nAin’t Too Proud is presented through special ar
 rangement with Music Theatre International \\(MTI\\). All authorized perfo
 rmance materials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com\n\nMusic Thea
 tre International gives Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times of the Tempt
 ations a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\, authentic look at the
  history of The Temptations. Parental discretion is advised.
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/broadway-under-the-star
 s-ain-t-too-proud-the-life-and-times-of-the-temp/18460828/2026-06-25T19
