BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain't Too Proud: The Life and Times of 
 the Temp.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T220000
UID:260330E3B0VOdcDEmt7RHVCJQITQ
DESCRIPTION:Ain’t Too Proud is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musical 
 that follows The Temptations’ extraordinary journey from the streets of 
 Detroit to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance m
 oves and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind the
  music: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success the
 y achieved \\(42 Top Ten hits\, 14 \\#1 singles\\)\, and the personal and 
 political tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in A
 merica.\n\nThis thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betray
 al is set to the beat of the group’s treasured hits\, including “My Gi
 rl\,” “Just My Imagination\,” “Get Ready\,” “Papa Was a Rollin
 g Stone” and so many more\, with a book by award-winning playwright Domi
 nique Morisseau \\(Skeleton Crew\, Paradise Blue\\) adapted from Williams
 ’s 1988 memoir. The New York Times praised the show as\, “Pretty clos
 e to perfect”\, with The Washington Post proclaiming it was “Dazzling 
 and Electrifying.”\n\nAin’t Too Proud is presented through special ar
 rangement with Music Theatre International \\(MTI\\). All authorized perfo
 rmance materials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com\n\nMusic Thea
 tre International gives Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times of the Tempt
 ations a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\, authentic look at the
  history of The Temptations. Parental discretion is advised.
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/broadway-under-the-star
 s-ain-t-too-proud-the-life-and-times-of-the-temp/18460828/2026-06-26T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LEARN TO ROW **North Bay Rowing Club Summer Camp
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T120000
UID:260309V6xDI5DLXUma9pBIZEikFg
DESCRIPTION:**Learn-to-Row Summer Camp Information - North Bay Rowing Club
 **\n\nAt the **Learn-to-Row** **Summer Camp**\, athletes will learn the 
 fundamentals of the sport both on land and on the water. They will meet cu
 rrent members of the team who will help guide and instruct them in proper 
 form\, and learn what it means to be a part of a team. Athletes will begin
  instruction on-land learning proper boat handling and basic sculling tech
 nique\, and then they will practice their skills on-water in singles and t
 eam boats that holds either 2 or 4 students in a shell. Students may have 
 the opportunity to learn more about racing skills and perform short distan
 ce races at the end of the week-long session.\n\nSummer camps are open to
  ***all*** rowers\, whether you're a looking to explore a new sport or s
 imply looking for a fun activity! No experience is required!\n\n**Athletes
 **: 13-17 years\n\n**Prerequisite:** No experience is required!!\n\n**Sess
 ion Days:** Monday through Friday\n\n**Session Times :** 9:00am -12:00pm
 \n\n**Learn To Row Session Dates:** Session 1: June 22 - 26 Session 2: Jul
 y 6 - 10 Session 3: July 13 - 17 Session 4: July 20 - 24 Session 5: July 2
 7 - 31
LOCATION:North Bay Rowing Club
URL:https://www.northbayrowing.org/2026-summer-camps/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
