BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Acoustic Sunsets at Sonoma Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260626T000000
UID:260612FFNbxcotYU-crIek7jzk6A
DESCRIPTION:Acoustic Sunsets returns for its third season at Sonoma Botani
 cal Garden in Glen Ellen. Every Wednesday evening from May through mid-Sep
 tember\, the Garden extends its hours and fills its outdoor amphitheater w
 ith live music by Bay Area musicians. Guests can bring picnics\, enjoy win
 e tastings with local Sonoma County vintners\, and unwind among the lush g
 rounds. Well-behaved dogs on leash are welcome. The series runs May 6 thro
 ugh September 16\, 2026\, with performances from 5:30 to 7:30 p.m. Admissi
 on is $17 for adults\, $14 for seniors\, and $8 for youth. Free for Garden
  members. New this year\, monthly Noche Latina nights celebrate Latin musi
 c and culture alongside a special exhibition of sculptural works.  Visit W
 ebsite  Event Tickets
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/acoustic-sunsets-at-sonoma-botanical-gard
 en-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T170000
UID:260529ynAYkzhPP06h-f3Y_0yl3g
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
