BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Shop of Horrors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T193000
UID:260528ncL1PnA0UEeucwe7gq6KLg
DESCRIPTION:Howard Ashman and Alan Menken gave the world this camp classic
  in 1982. They based musical (loosely) on the low-budget 1960 black comedy
  film *The Little Shop of Horrors*\, with Menken’s score featuring spec
 tacular music: early 1960s-style rock and roll\, doo-wop\, and early Motow
 n.\n\nThe story centers on meek floral assistant Seymour Krelborn\, who st
 umbles across a new breed of plant he names “Audrey II” after his cowo
 rker crush. This foul-mouthed\, R&B-singing carnivore promises unending fa
 me and fortune to the down-and-out Krelborn as long as he keeps feeding it
  BLOOD. Over time\, though\, Seymour discovers Audrey II’s out-of-this-w
 orld origins and its intent toward global domination!\n\n**June 26\, 27\, 
 28\; July 2\\*\, 3\, 5\, 9\, 10\, 11\, 12**\n\n**Friday and Saturday Shows
 :** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Matinee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 
 PM\n\nBook and Lyrics by Howard Ashman\n\nMusic By Alan Menken  \n\nDirec
 tor                  Katie Watts-Whitaker\n\nMusic Direct
 or        Kelly Considine\n\nChoreographer       Katie Watts-Wh
 itaker
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/little-shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Bloom Fest Open Farm Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T160000
UID:260523hyi910YVRk2dNsX9gTeBQw
DESCRIPTION:Mid-May to mid-July is the time when all the lavender at Bees 
 N Blooms is blooming with bright purple radiance\, and we open the farm to
  the public for Lavender Bloom Fest!\n\n**Lavender Bloom Fest Field Days:*
 * May 23\, May 30-31\, June 6-7\, June 13-14\, June 20\,\n\n**Lavender Su
 nset Evenings:** May\, 29\, June 5\, June 12\, June 19\, June 26\n\n**Jaz
 z Days:** May 24\, June 21\, and July 12\n\n**Lavender U-Cut Experience:*
 * June 27-28\, July 4-5\, July 11. Note: July 12 is also a U-Cut day\, bu
 t is listed under Jazz Days.\n\nBring the kids\, visit the poultry palace\
 , play farm bingo\, and snap a picture in the giant lavender chair! Shop t
 he Farm Stand and visit the Bees N Blooms Nursery. Sunset evenings are spe
 cial at Bees N Blooms. Enjoy the view as the suns shines a golden light on
  the lavender. Enjoy dinner with Tacos don Pepe\, then head to the labyrin
 th to watch the sunset.
LOCATION:Bees N Blooms
URL:https://beesnblooms.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - School Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T113000
UID:260523F_fptJZ69Eyts9vfCZPQIA
DESCRIPTION:**Teachers\, Text Books and School Spirit**\n\nSchools have lo
 ng been of key importance in Healdsburg. **Steve** **Deas** will look at t
 he early days of education\, when farm kids got their basic education in o
 ne-room country school houses and the Seventh Day Adventist community esta
 blished a college that sat near the center of town. Then he'll talk about 
 more modern schools and their importance in the community. And we'll ask t
 he audience to share stories of favorite teachers\, classroom hijinks and 
 school spirit.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Sip & Seek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T160000
UID:260522km15LGdSJUWX791XudimZg
DESCRIPTION:A wine country scavenger hunt for explorers\, wine lovers and 
 weekend adventurers alike. Journey through some of West County's most beau
 tiful wineries while snapping selfies along the way.\n\nEach winery has ch
 osen a unique feature to be discovered. Find it\, snap a photo and tag the
  winery and @tastewestcounty to share your adventure with us and be entere
 d to win a gift. Gather your friends and get ready for some summer vibes
LOCATION:Paul Mathew
URL:http://tastewestcounty.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T180000
UID:260515lXopfe-lO0O5Q6pe2gW1hg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\n**JUNE EXHIBIT: SUMME
 RTIME LIVIN’ EASY**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 1 – June 28\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gra
 y  and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show a
 nd the Gallery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery
 ’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Re
 freshments will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fi
 zz.**\n\nSonoma County artist\, **Nancy Gray\,** unveils new summer-inspir
 ed acrylic paintings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the 
 region’s beauty.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows
 . Drawing inspiration from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abou
 nd with interpretive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal colo
 r expression plays out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue t
 endrils of shade dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a 
 carpet of golden yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splen
 dor\,”amplifying the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dra
 matic contrasting role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play again
 st the purplish blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by t
 he landscape\, these works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  
 “We are blessed to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – ever
 ywhere I look\, I see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelo
 ng passion for art.  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country wi
 th its inspirational landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early
  years vacationing on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright
  color palette.  She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90
 ’s and continued to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.
   Gray exhibits regionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gall
 ery for five years.\n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June
  18 and 25 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features
  **Collective Expressions: 29 Years\,** a members’ collaborative show ce
 lebrating the Gallery’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an excit
 ing mix of mediums\, subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery
 ’s dynamic diversity.  Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich hig
 hlight our region’s beauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\;
  from sunflowers to roses\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller
 \, Schaffer\, Sumner and Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolp
 er’s stunning still-life\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charles
 ton’s jewelry\; abstracts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary
  complement\; figurative works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this cl
 assic to contemporary overview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso jo
 in us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART 
 NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community ev
 ent celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. 
  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Hea
 ldsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **ww
 w.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly 
 Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Great Gatsby- No SALSA EVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T200000
UID:260511dzgZrzf9rkaUOZsk3DZ6Eg
DESCRIPTION:Step back into the “Roaring Twenties” for an evening of un
 matched glamour and old-world prestige. We invite you to a night inspired 
 by the legendary Jay Gatsby—where the champagne flows like water and the
  jazz never stops.\n\nDine and dance amidst a backdrop of black and gold\,
  Art Deco decadence\, and shimmering crystal. It’s time to celebrate wit
 h the kind of “careless intensity” that only the Jazz Age can provide.
 \n\nThe Vibe\n\n• The Soundtrack: Fast-paced “Electro-Swing” \\(thin
 k modern beats mixed with 1920s brass\\) or a live brass band playing Char
 leston-style jazz.\n\n• The Theme: An era of shimmering gold and rhythmi
 c jazz where the champagne flows like water and the night belongs to the b
 eautiful and the damned.\n\n• Special Guest: the incredible James Darlin
 g.\n\n• Fuel: Complimentary wine and snacks to keep you “Getting Jiggy
  Wit It” \\(while supplies last\\).\n\nThe Details\n\n• When: June 27 
 | 6:00 PM – 8:00 PM\n\n• Where: Salsa Dance Marin | 4140 Redwood Hwy 8
 \, San Rafael \\(Upstairs\\)\n\n• Who: Everyone is welcome! 21\\+\n\nPri
 ce\n\nEarly bird $20\, last minute $30\, at the door $45
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/great-gatsby/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MusicTime in the Library with Festival Napa Valley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
UID:260508tep1_mfI7EiP0HYUQPZRzg
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy fun\, interactive concerts for kids \\(ages 2-8\\) and t
 heir adults.
LOCATION:Napa County Library
URL:https://events.napalibrary.org/event/16297546
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T170000
UID:260508QHgw42zHEEaO4XKo5MNIHQ
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibition Opening: Christo and Jeanne-Claude: Running Fence at 50
  Years
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T170000
UID:260508LOXb_8SoQkKhrJfID2yzdw
DESCRIPTION:This landmark exhibition celebrates the 50th anniversary of C
 hristo and Jeanne-Claude’s monumental *Running Fence*\, the temporary a
 rt installation that stretched over 24 miles through Sonoma and Marin Coun
 ties. The project became world famous\, and is an iconic part of North Bay
  culture and history.\n\nThrough immersive design\, powerful visuals\, and
  firsthand accounts\, the exhibit invites visitors to experience the magic
  and beauty that was the *Running Fence* – white fabric flowing across
  fields and cresting over hills to vanish into the Pacific Ocean – and t
 o discover the remarkable 4-year odyssey that brought it to fruition. Admi
 ssion for sale at the door.
LOCATION:Museums of Sonoma County
URL:https://museumsc.org/events/?eid=12890
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spirit Guides Guided Walking Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T113000
UID:260427-l751zsYkESjMkzaNQ7bOg
DESCRIPTION:Join knowledgeable volunteer Garden Guides for special tours o
 f Spirit Guides at Sonoma Botanical Garden on select Saturdays during the 
 run of the exhibition. Experience the updated entrance to our California O
 aks Trail and discover the vibrant\, monumental sculptures by Jacobo and M
 aría Ángeles\, hearing stories about the works’ cultural inspirations\
 , symbolic meanings\, and connections with the natural world. Our voluntee
 rs will enrich your visit with insights into the artists’ process\, the 
 Zapotec influences behind the spirit animals\, and how the exhibition comp
 lements the surrounding landscape. These engaging English language tours o
 ffer context and conversation that deepen your appreciation of both the ar
 t and the Garden.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Morning Hike and Tasting at the Ridge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T110000
UID:260420AalCpm39xUuYyR-OfhxaQg
DESCRIPTION:As featured in San Francisco Chronicle list of “10 wine tast
 ings in Napa and Sonoma with ‘wellness’ activities like hiking\, bikin
 g and yoga”\n\nEmbark on a guided “grape-to-glass” journey that begi
 ns with artisan trail treats before ascending into our dramatically terrac
 ed hillside vineyards.\n\nAs you navigate the estate\, your host will prov
 ide deep insights into our diverse ecosystems and the geological significa
 nce of our Stags Leap District location. You will explore why these distin
 ct sites produce such storied wines while enjoying a comparative tasting t
 hat showcases the nuance and variation across our premier appellations.\n\
 n**Pricing:** $100 per guest | $80 per club member\n\n**Availability:** Gr
 oups of 1–12 guests\n\n**Pace:** Moderate hike with challenging inclines
 \; weather permitting\n\n**Attire:** Strictly no open-toed shoes. Appropri
 ate hiking footwear is require
LOCATION:Pine Ridge Vineyards
URL:https://www.pineridgevineyards.com/events/morning-hike-and-tasting-at-
 the-ridge/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T000000
UID:260416MYKoLb3410KD6_u-dtWNng
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Belly Left Coast Kitchen & Taproom
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108193422?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
