BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miniature Worlds from Recycled Materials
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T120000
UID:260612nk-eG1QnFkSBzoRhi-JT7g
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nIn this 3-hour hands-on workshop\, participants will exp
 lore the art of transforming recycled materials into imaginative miniature
  worlds. Using a wide variety of found and repurposed objects\, students w
 ill experiment with scale\, texture\, and composition as they design and b
 uild their own tiny scenes\, discovering how the magic of these creations 
 live in the smallest details they choose to include. Alongside the creativ
 e process\, the workshop will include moments of reflection and group shar
 ing\, encouraging participants to think about storytelling\, personal expr
 ession\, and the possibilities of everyday materials. This playful and tho
 ughtful experience is designed to spark creativity\, build confidence\, an
 d invite artists of all levels to approach materials in new and imaginativ
 e ways.\n\nThis class is located in the Classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: 
 \n\nEsther Hilsenrad is a Bay Area&ndash\;based artist and educator origin
 ally from New York City\, with over 23 years of teaching experience across
  a wide range of subjects and age groups. Her career has spanned formal cl
 assroom teaching\, museum education\, and work as a teaching artist. Now w
 orking independently\, Esther teaches art camps from her home studio\, aft
 erschool art classes\, and private lessons for elementary-aged children. H
 er deepest passion lies in art education&mdash\;guiding others to feel con
 fident expressing themselves creatively and exploring diverse artistic med
 iums. In her own artistic practice\, Esther enjoys experimenting with colo
 r theory through acrylic painting\, crafting miniature scenes from recycle
 d materials\, and creating jewelry and other crafts. Her work is driven by
  a genuine love of both making art and helping others discover their creat
 ive voice.\n\nLearn more: \n\nwww.esthertheartteacher.com \n\nwww.estherhe
 artsart.com\n\n@estherheartsart\n\n@esthertheartteacher
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-miniature-world
 s?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Cloisonné
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T160000
UID:260612XnBcWPsYj0Orl4rcZqMAJw
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nStep into the luminous world of cloisonn&eacute\; in thi
 s engaging workshop with artist Paul LaPorte. Discover the history and int
 ricate process behind this ancient enameling technique as he showcases fin
 ished works and reveals how delicate wires\, vibrant ground glass\, and re
 peated kiln firings come together to create richly colored\, jewel-like su
 rfaces. You'll get to observe demonstrations of the cloisonn&eacute\; and 
 enameling process&mdash\;from shaping the tiny metal cells to polishing th
 e final piece to a brilliant luster--and try your hand at some stage of th
 e work.\n\nThis dynamic introduction offers a rare behind-the-scenes peek 
 at a meticulous craft&mdash\;perfect for anyone who is ready to try the an
 cient art of enameling. If there is interest in engaging more fully in mas
 tering this craft\, you can sign up for a follow-up series of classes bein
 g offered by Paul LaPorte at PAC.\n\nThis workshop is located in the class
 room.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nPaul LaPorte is a cloisonn&eacute\; enamel
 ist whose work is shaped by a lifelong focus on observation\, place\, and 
 material precision. His interest in enameling began in Key West during his
  Navy service\, later leading him to earn a BFA from the California Colleg
 e of the Arts and study with Marin-based enamelist Diane Merrill. He pursu
 ed graduate work in Metal Arts at San Francisco State University and recei
 ved an Annette Kade Grant to study in France\, where time in Provence deep
 ened his sensitivity to color\, line\, and landscape. Alongside a 20-year 
 career as a tour manager across the American West\, his work has remained 
 rooted in careful observation. Today\, he shares his expertise through tea
 ching cloisonn&eacute\; enameling.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-cloisonne?aff=
 cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
